saveJournal call sites corrected to 23 — grep -c gives 16 in engine.go (exit 0) and 7 in staging.go (exit 0); cycle 2 wrote 24/8 while listing only seven staging anchors, so the arithmetic was wrong and the anchors were right. Corrected in Sec 2.2 (now a per-file table) and Sec 6; the two copy-loop sites staging.go:141/:161 retained. (3) Patch B1 made implementable: scenario.classes is read at commit_atomicity_test.go:163 (injection loop) AND :206 (full-coverage assertion), so a second field is mandatory. Sec 4.2 now gives literal B1.a-B1.e — add injectClasses []string, leave classes untouched, replace sharedUserHome bool with userHome string, both constructors take injectClass string, and the scenario table is GENERATED by ranging over projectSweepClasses/globalSweepClasses so full class coverage holds structurally rather than by grep. New Sec 4.2.1 is the function-level identifier allowlist (7 entries, nothing else may be introduced); no new imports needed and fixture_test.go stays off the patch list. (4) The blanket no-assertion-removed claim is withdrawn as self-contradictory. New Sec 5.1 treats the cross-class residue chain as INTENTIONALLY RETIRED defence in depth: 31 ordered class pairs (21 project + 10 global) drop to 0; what still proves the property directly is before.diff(snapshotState) at :178 on every injection; what is genuinely lost is a defect that both escapes snapshotState hand-maintained path list AND only manifests through a later class; cycle-2 sanction recorded as attributable; two-class fallback (restores 9 of 31 pairs, ~384s race) named as escalation, not recommendation. Sec 4 preamble and Sec 9 risk 5 restated to match. NEW cycle-3 findings not requested by review: (a) Estimate C downgraded — its non-race denominator 228.344s comes from a 25-line truncated log whose line 21 is FAIL internal/godriver 99.383s (two subtests dying on go-v1 process_timeout, a host-load symptom), and .temp/TASK-260720-2284br/worktree has since been RESET to 4 test