o the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B. Items 13/14 checked as producer-side self-assessment: every producer-owned AC clause is satisfied; the AC final clause (reviewer independently checks the plan) is by construction the next cycle gate and is tracked by item 16. Outcome resources: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md updated in place (SHA-256 d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b) and NEW TASK-260729-3dr6hw_cycle3-rework-record.md. Logbook entry 2026-07-29 1756.\nHANDOFF NOTE cycle 3 — task-board handoff --role researcher was run and REFUSED with real exit 1: "cannot hand off TASK-260729-3dr6hw: unchecked checklist items [15] (Tests green): handoff evidence missing". Status was therefore set to to-review explicitly. Item 15 stays unchecked on purpose: no Go test, build or vet command has been executed in any of the three cycles of this task, and the task scope forbids running the full or race suite, so there is no exit-0 command behind that item and checking it would be a false green under the Evidence Honesty Contract. Item 15 belongs to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B and runs the section 7 focused commands. Unlike cycle 2, items 13 and 14 ARE now checked, as the producer-side self-assessment they are — every producer-owned AC clause is satisfied and the AC final clause (reviewer independently checks the plan) is by construction the next cycle gate, tracked by item 16. Reviewer, please verify in this order: (1) that internal/install/cache_conformance_test.go and dryrun_conformance_test.go really are candidate-only, so the corrected 34-line rsync expectation and the statement that only the Sec 8.2 SHA-256 manifest covers them are both right; (2) grep -c saveJournal on internal/transaction/engine.go and staging.go, expecting 16 and 7; (3) that Patch B1 as written in Sec 4.2 compiles conceptually — injectClasses at :163, classes untouched at :206, the generated scenario table, and that the Sec 4.2.1 identifier allowlist is complete; (4) whether the Sec 5.1 framing of the retired cross-class chain is the honest description you asked for, including the named residual exposure and the two-class fallback; (5) the cycle-3 Estimate C downgrade and whether the new Sec 3.5 same-run mechanism corroboration is sound. Deliverable: .research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md, SHA-256 d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b, attached as outcome resource TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md; cycle-3 change record attached as TASK-260729-3dr6hw_cycle3-rework-record.md. No candidate file was modified and no Go command was executed.\nagent completed: [analyst] researcher (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-6eee2a, pid=13097, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-330d04, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-330d04)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 — CHANGES REQUESTED to analysis. Cycle-2 corrections and the producer plan are independently confirmed. One bounded evidence repair remains in newly added section 3.5: it omits internal/runtimestore (18.630s non-race, 18.244s race, x0.98) while claiming every meaningful completed package is listed, and it incorrectly attributes internal/transaction x1.25 to git/go-build subprocess time despite only two test-binary re-exec sites and no git/go-build test invocation. Correct or remove that causal claim, preserve the accepted plan, and return for review. Evidence: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_review-verdict-cycle-3.md. No candidate edit or Go command was performed.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-330d04, pid=19473, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-840b17, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-840b17)\nCycle 4 (researcher) — bounded evidence repair of §3.5 per the cycle-3 verdict. Ready for review.\n\nCorrection 1 (selection rule / omitted package): VERIFIED TRUE. internal/runtimestore completed both sides at 18.630s -> 18.244s = x0.98 and was omitted. §3.5 now states a mechanical rule (completed ok on both gates AND max(non-race, race) >= 10s), applied to all 38 both-side-completed packages, yielding exactly 5. All five listed: cmd/curator x1.45, godriver x1.39, transaction x1.25, runtimestore x0.98, managerlock x2.90. The word every is withdrawn and the x1.25-1.45 claim is stated as false. Second omission found and disclosed: managerlock is under 10s non-race but 15.542s under race, so it enters under max() at x2.90 — the largest >10s completed factor and a direct counterexample. Completed range under the rule is x0.98-x2.90; across all 38 it is x0.78 (capabilities) to x8.47 (buildmeta).\n\nCorrection 2 (subprocess attribution): VERIFIED TRUE and the claim is withdrawn entirely for all three packages, not softened for one. internal/transaction has 50 tests, ~33 Prepare sites, exactly 2 exec.Command sites (subprocess_test.go:56,459, both re-executing the test binary) and zero git / go build invocations — an in-process package at x1.25, which refutes cycle 3s in-process => large inflation story. managerlock is also in-process, has zero time.Sleep in tests, and reads x2.90. §3.5 is now explicitly descriptive, carries a static-inventory table with the caveat that call-site counts are not wall-time shares, and takes the reviewers permitted alternative: workload shape via journal target count P (alarm dumps record P=8 for install, P=19/20 for atomicity; transactions Prepare literals hold one to a few targets), labelled a hypothesis predicting direction not magnitude.\n\nCycle-4 findings not requested: (1) atomicitys same-run ratio 603.701/441.122 = x1.37 is censored and lower than cmd/curators x1.45 purely from truncation — now marked as carrying no information, pointing at §3.4s phase-level solve; (2) the same withdrawn causal claim existed in §2.2 and §3.3 closing clauses and was repaired there too, otherwise the §3.5 fix would be cosmetic; (3) §3.1s status row for the mechanism downgraded from measured to hypothesis; (4) new §9 risk 6 records the mechanism as unmeasured and names the cheap confirmation (focused -race -cpuprofile of the atomicity sweep) as outside this tasks no-execution boundary. Old risk 6 renumbered to 7; no cross-reference pointed at it.\n\nPreserved unchanged: §1 timeout inventory, §2.1/§2.3-2.5 hot-path evidence, §4 patch (88/19 Patch A split, Patch B injectClasses selector, generated per-class scenarios, distinct global user homes), §4.0 13-file allowlist with aba_test.go and atomicity/fixture_test.go excluded, §5/§5.1 assertion matrix and retired-invariant disclosure, §7 focused commands and 480s bar, §8 candidate-integrity gates, §6 out-of-scope production finding, and every timing band.\n\nEvidence honesty: no go test/build/vet command was run in any cycle of this task; no candidate file was edited. Two non-zero exits this cycle, both grep zero-match (transaction git/go-build probe, managerlock time.Sleep probe), reported as-is. Checklist item 15 (Tests green) stays UNCHECKED — no green Go command exists behind it and the task forbids running the suite; it belongs to the downstream producer.\n\nDeliverable: .research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md, SHA-256 46316048a5eec0f45c48d34d4dc2751c19a2b7790ddbba1dda85dd0474cf45cb (cycle-3 was d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b). Board resource updated in place; cycle-4 rework record attached.\nHANDOFF NOTE cycle 4 — task-board handoff --role researcher was run standalone and REFUSED with real exit 1: cannot hand off TASK-260729-3dr6hw: unchecked checklist items [15] (Tests green): handoff evidence missing. Status set to to-review explicitly, same as cycles 2 and 3. Item 15 stays unchecked on purpose: no Go test, build or vet command has been executed in any of the four cycles of this task, the task scope forbids running the full or race suite, and there is no exit-0 command behind that item — checking it would be a false green under the Evidence Honesty Contract. It belongs to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B and runs the section 7 focused commands.\n\nReviewer, cycle 4 was a bounded evidence repair only. Please verify in this order:\n(1) The section 3.5 selection rule — completed ok on BOTH verifier-3 gates AND max(non-race, race) >= 10s — really does yield exactly the five listed packages when applied to all 38 both-side-completed packages, and that internal/managerlock (5.366s to 15.542s = x2.90) belongs in the table under max(). It was not named in the cycle-3 verdict; it entered because the corrected rule admits it, and it is the strongest counterexample to the withdrawn homogeneity claim.\n(2) That the subprocess mechanism attribution is withdrawn everywhere, not only in section 3.5: the closing clauses of sections 2.2 and 3.3 and the mechanism row of the section 3.1 status table all carried it and were all repaired.\n(3) That the workload-shape reframing is labelled a hypothesis throughout and that no number in sections 3.2 or 3.4 depends on it — the bands, the 1000s sizing figure, and the atomicity 1284-1494s band are unchanged.\n(4) That marking the atomicity same-run ratio x1.37 as censored and information-free is correct, and that routing the reader to the secti