.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-2284br_commit-installations-atomically/progress.md:148:Rework cycle 4 (R5) in progress 2026-07-28. R5 root cause accepted and reversed at the read: the four declaration observations digested the path as an operation separate from the parse, and every supported writer rewrites its manifest in place with os.WriteFile, so an A -> B -> A rewrite around the read left both samples at A while the closure came from the transient B. Fix: one read owns both bytes and generation. New internal/install/generation.go readDocument opens once, hands the returned payload to the parser, and records the generation OF THOSE BYTES; manifest.ParseBytes, devsub.ParseBytes and scopes.ParseHybridDecls are the byte-level entry points their own Load functions now delegate to, so no loader reads a path twice. observations became one record per key (generation + path + reader) and declaration keys got their own documentKey type, so a document can only enter through observeDocument and never through the path-digest observe. Negative control both directions: with the pre-fix relation restored all four install-level ABA cases fail and commit the transient declaration, while the byte-identical-rewrite control still passes.
